## 9. Example Cisco Router Configuration

The commands below illustrate how the routing concepts can be implemented.

Interface names and IP assignments must be checked against the actual router models and saved Packet Tracer configurations.

### Core Router Configuration

```cisco
enable
configure terminal

! Laptop LAN
interface GigabitEthernet0/0
 ip address 10.10.10.1 255.255.255.0
 no shutdown
exit

! Server LAN
interface GigabitEthernet0/1
 ip address 10.10.20.1 255.255.255.0
 no shutdown
exit

! Connection to BR1
interface GigabitEthernet1/0
 ip address 150.150.150.1 255.255.255.0
 no shutdown
exit

! Connection to BR2
interface GigabitEthernet1/1
 ip address 200.200.200.1 255.255.255.0
 no shutdown
exit

! Connection to ISP
interface GigabitEthernet1/2
 ip address 100.100.100.1 255.255.255.0
 no shutdown
exit

! Static route to BR1 LAN
ip route 10.10.30.0 255.255.255.0 150.150.150.2

! Static route to BR2 LAN
ip route 10.10.40.0 255.255.255.0 200.200.200.2

! Default route toward ISP
ip route 0.0.0.0 0.0.0.0 100.100.100.2

end
copy running-config startup-config
```

