## 11. Network Verification

After configuring the routers, it is important to verify their interfaces, routing tables, and network connectivity.

### Check Interface Status

```cisco
show ip interface brief
```

This command displays:

- Interface names.
- Assigned IP addresses.
- Administrative status.
- Line protocol status.

An operational interface normally displays:

```text
up    up
```

If an interface displays:

```text
administratively down    down
```

it can be enabled using:

```cisco
configure terminal
interface GigabitEthernet0/0
no shutdown
```

### Verify Static Routes

```cisco
show ip route static
```

This command displays installed static routes.

### Check Running Configuration

```cisco
show running-config
```

This command displays the active router configuration.

### Check Startup Configuration

```cisco
show startup-config
```

This command displays the saved configuration stored in NVRAM.

### Save the Configuration

```cisco
copy running-config startup-config
```

This saves the active configuration so it can be restored after a router reload.

