## 15. Key Networking Concepts Demonstrated

### Static Routing

Manual configuration of routes to reach remote networks.

### Administrative Distance

A numeric value that determines route-source preference when eligible routes to the same destination prefix compete.

### Floating Static Routes

Backup routes configured with a higher Administrative Distance than primary routes.

### Default Routing

A route used when no more specific matching route exists.

### Next-Hop Address

The neighboring router IP address used to forward packets toward a remote destination.

### Directly Connected Networks

Networks automatically added to the routing table when a router interface is configured and operational.

### Routing Tables

Data structures used by routers to determine forwarding paths.

### Network Redundancy

Using multiple potential paths to improve network availability.

### Failover

Switching to an alternative path when the primary route becomes unavailable.

### Troubleshooting

Using Cisco IOS commands to identify and resolve networking issues.

